-- title:
--   Component ideals at η(v): maximal, others the unit ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{X}$ for $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) (finiteness of the node index set, existence of oriented crossing charts over the base change, the étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of the assignment of node points, closedness of each node point in $X_O$, and the model hypotheses for $O$), and assume that each of the points $\xi_j$ lies in the open $\mathrm{X}_0$ of the associated chart input $C$, i.e. avoids all node points. Write $Y$ for the glued scheme obtained from these data and, for each component index $v$, let $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ be the ideal sheaf datum on $Y$ given by [`V3Glue.ChartInput.compG`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_ResolvedModelGlueComponents.html#L40), namely the vanishing ideal of the closure of the point $\eta(v)$. The assertion is: for every $v$ there exist an affine open $U$ of $Y$ containing $\eta(v)$ such that the ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{Y,\eta(v)}$ generated by the image, under the germ map from $\Gamma(Y,U)$, of the ideal $\mathrm{comp}(v)(U)$ equals the maximal ideal of that stalk, while for every $w \neq v$ the ideal so generated by $\mathrm{comp}(w)(U)$ is the unit ideal.
--
--   This says that each $\eta(v)$ is a generic point of its own component of the special fibre of the resolved model — the component's ideal cuts out exactly the closed point of the stalk there — and that the remaining components do not pass through $\eta(v)$. It is one of the fields verified in the assembly of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ with its étale crossing charts, used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts).
